WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.129
Every OSINT workflow should start with a clear intelligence requirement: the question the work must answer for a named decision or operational need.

00:00:10.129 --> 00:00:15.297
A vague request such as research this company invites uncontrolled searching.

00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:21.292
A useful requirement identifies the subject, timeframe, decision, and required level of confidence.

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:26.460
Identify who needs the answer and how it will be used.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.628
An incident responder may need a rapid assessment within an hour.

00:00:31.628 --> 00:00:37.623
A due-diligence team may accept a longer timeline but require documented primary sources.

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:41.964
Audience and consequence determine depth, format, review, and escalation.

00:00:41.964 --> 00:00:43.824
Define scope explicitly.

00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:50.646
In-scope elements may include public infrastructure, official records, or published statements within a date range.

00:00:50.646 --> 00:01:01.602
Out-of-scope elements may include personal data unrelated to the purpose, private accounts, restricted systems, or activity requiring legal authority that the team does not possess.

00:01:01.602 --> 00:01:08.011
Record constraints such as deadline, language, geography, approved tools, budget, privacy rules, and retention.

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:11.938
State assumptions and terms that could be ambiguous.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:20.414
A clear definition of the entity prevents records from different people or organizations with similar names from being merged.

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:23.928
Specify what a satisfactory answer looks like.

00:01:23.928 --> 00:01:29.509
This may include confirmed findings, assessed possibilities, important gaps, and recommended validation.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:40.466
Set stopping conditions so the team can conclude when the question has been answered to the required level or when available public information is insufficient.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:46.460
Requirements can change as evidence appears, but changes should be documented and approved.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:51.215
This preserves accountability and prevents quiet expansion into unrelated collection.

00:01:51.215 --> 00:01:58.450
The requirement remains the anchor for deciding whether each search, source, and reported detail is necessary.
